# AI Client DFY And DWY System

MedSpa Growth Engine should be done-for-you for the clinic owner, but it should still include done-with-you moments where the clinic provides access, confirms preferences, and approves sensitive communication.

This file defines what the AI operator handles for clients after they buy.

## Client Experience Promise

The clinic should feel:

- They are not buying another dashboard to manage.
- They are getting a recovery operator installed around their existing process.
- They know what is happening every week.
- They only get asked for decisions when needed.
- Their team does not have to learn a complicated platform.

## DFY vs DWY Split

| Area | DFY - we do it | DWY - client helps/approves |
|---|---|---|
| Intake | Create checklist, chase missing items, organize assets | Provide clinic info, tools, branding, access |
| Workflow setup | Configure workflows, dashboard, Sheets, reports | Approve workflow timing and contact rules |
| Messaging | Draft review, referral, no-show, and reactivation copy | Approve voice, restricted phrases, and offer details |
| Testing | Run internal QA and error checks | Confirm test messages and booking flow |
| Launch | Prepare handoff and weekly reporting | Approve go-live |
| Monitoring | Watch errors, reporting, recovery signals, churn risk | Respond to escalations |
| Improvement | Suggest campaigns and retention ideas | Approve campaigns and any client-facing changes |

## Client AI Operator Roles

### Onboarding Assistant

Output:

- Access checklist.
- Missing information reminders.
- Kickoff summary.
- Client success metric.
- Scope confirmation.

### Workflow QA Assistant

Output:

- Workflow test plan.
- Error handling check.
- Dashboard status check.
- Report status check.
- Go-live blocker list.

### Recovery Monitor

Output:

- Missed inquiry status.
- No-show recovery status.
- Lapsed VIP movement.
- Review/referral workflow activity.
- Weekly report status.

### Client Success Assistant

Output:

- Weekly client update.
- Monthly health score.
- Churn-risk signals.
- Next improvement idea.
- Renewal or upsell timing.

## Client Autopilot Loops

| Loop | Trigger | AI action | Client/owner handoff |
|---|---|---|---|
| Missing access | Intake item missing after 24 hours | Draft reminder and update blocker list | Owner sends or approves |
| Workflow error | Error handler fires | Summarize issue and severity | Owner fixes or escalates |
| Weekly report | Weekly report due | Draft wins and recovery summary | Owner reviews before sending if needed |
| Low activity | No meaningful system movement | Suggest campaign or client check-in | Owner/client approves |
| Churn risk | Errors, silence, or low visibility | Create save-plan note | Owner handles relationship |
| Upsell trigger | Stable client plus extra opportunity | Draft improvement recommendation | Owner decides offer |

## Client Weekly Report Standard

```text
Subject: Weekly recovery system update for [Clinic]

Hi [Name],

Here is what the recovery system checked this week:

Wins:
- [Win]
- [Win]

Recovery areas monitored:
- New inquiries:
- Booking confirmations:
- No-show recovery:
- Reviews/referrals:
- VIP/lapsed clients:

System health:
- Workflow status:
- Dashboard/reporting:
- Errors/blockers:

Next useful move:
- [One recommendation]

Owner action needed:
- [Only include when needed]
```

## Client Health Score

Score each live client weekly.

| Signal | Healthy | Watch | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|
| Weekly report | Sent | Late once | Missing |
| Workflow errors | None | One unresolved | Repeated |
| Client response | Engaged | Quiet | Avoiding |
| Recovery activity | Visible movement | Low movement | No movement |
| Blockers | None | Waiting client | Blocking launch/results |
| Sentiment | Positive | Neutral | Frustrated |

Risk response:

- Watch: send helpful update and one improvement.
- Risk: owner creates save plan and speaks with client.

## Client Boundaries

Included:

- Installed recovery workflows.
- Dashboard visibility.
- Weekly report.
- Light copy edits for installed flows.
- Error checks.
- Monthly improvement recommendation.

Not included without paid scope:

- New booking platform integration.
- SMS provider setup if not sold.
- Paid ads management.
- Custom analytics.
- Multi-location reporting.
- Medical/legal/compliance consulting.
- New workflows outside the sold recovery system.

## Client Handoff Rule

Clients should never feel abandoned after go-live.

Minimum post-launch cadence:

- Day 1: launch confirmation.
- Day 3: system health check.
- Day 7: first weekly report.
- Day 14: friction check.
- Day 30: monthly recovery review.

The AI prepares these. The owner sends or approves relationship-sensitive messages.
